WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.209
Three hundred and ninety-four unique entities.

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:06.397
One hundred and sixty-nine connection vectors.

00:00:06.397 --> 00:00:11.261
Five data dimensions: lobbying, voting, boards, funding, and procurement.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:16.454
This is the influence network topology — every relationship algorithmically mapped.

00:00:16.454 --> 00:00:20.193
Threat level scoring, normalized from zero to one.

00:00:20.193 --> 00:00:25.727
The MAID-Emergencies Nexus: threat score one point zero zero — the highest in the system.

00:00:25.727 --> 00:00:29.727
Foreign Influence Target Alpha: zero point nine eight.

00:00:29.727 --> 00:00:33.863
Queen's University Judicial Linkage: zero point nine nine.

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:37.579
CIJA Lobbying Pipeline: zero point nine five.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:41.386
CFNIS Proxy: zero point eight eight.

00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:43.681
The network is not a theory.

00:00:43.681 --> 00:00:48.579
It is a graph — built from five public datasets, cross-referenced algorithmically.

00:00:48.579 --> 00:00:57.022
When the same person appears on a corporate board, in a lobbying registration, and in a procurement contract with the department they used to run... that is a connection.

00:00:57.022 --> 00:01:00.624
And the algorithm found three hundred and ninety-four of them.
